WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.902
-Yeah!
-Hey. How you doing, man?

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.205
-Matt Bomer,
it's always great to see you.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.807
I was just talking to
Maya Rudolph.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.476
I think I still have glue
on my face from doing this.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.379
And we were
talking about Kamala.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.681
And last time you were here,

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.751
I made a pitch
that you should play Tom Brady.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:19.985
And I meant it.

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:22.789
And I was thinking, like,
is there any politician

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:25.825
that you think
you'd be good at playing?

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.294
-Well, first of all, I need to
start commissioning you,

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.897
because people come up to me
on the street

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.931
and think that that's
a real movie.

00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:35.301
And they ask for updates about
the Tom Brady biopic.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.869
-It should be
a Tom Brady biopic.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.704
There should be one.
-And I'm like, "Ask Jimmy."

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:41.140
-I'm good at this.
I have an idea.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.976
How about this?
-Yes.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.444
-I think you should do JFK.

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:48.648
-Yeah. I was going to say
it would have to be a Kennedy.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.149
That would be the dream.
-Or JFK Jr.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:51.350
-I really believe that.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.953
-I love that American dynasty
kind of thing

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.054
that they got going on.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.856
That's it.
-I think you could crush it.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.458
-That's it.
Let's put it out there.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:00.760
-We're going to
put it out there.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.163
I'm telling you, there is
at least four Kennedy movies

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.198
in the works, getting ready
right now.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.667
I know for a fact.
-Yeah.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.171
-So, Matt Bomer
would be perfect to play,

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.504
really, any of the Kennedys.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.673
-Alright. I'm in. I'm in.
-Alright, I put it out there.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.775
Let me know what happens.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.476
Oh, this is
going to be exciting.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.945
You're quarantining
with your husband

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.447
and your three teenage sons.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:22.748
-Yes.
-You posted this.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:25.918
I follow your -- You're great on
Instagram, by the way.

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.853
-Oh, thanks, man.
-And I love following you.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.290
And one of the things
that you said --

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.957
the best things you watched
in quarantine

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:34.027
was the
Beastie Boys documentary.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.297
-Oh.
-That was -- that was great.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.698
Are you -- Were you
a big fan growing up?

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.000
-Huge fan.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.902
I mean, I'll never forget --
it's so iconic to me,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:46.138
when my brother got the
"Licensed to Ill" tape.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.172
-Yeah.
-That's how old I am.

00:01:47.172 --> 00:01:48.474
-It was the tape.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.944
-And I knew how to, like,
turn it around to rewind it

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.645
to get right back to
the beginning of the song

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.513
on the other side,
because I didn't have

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.881
the boom box
that had rewind on it.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:57.317
-So you fast-forwarded it?

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.218
-Remember you used to have to
flip it around and fast-forward?

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:01.320
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.455
-We used to do that.
That's such a great reference.

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:06.559
-Dude, the best.
And they just blew my mind, man.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.262
I mean, I'm still
such a huge fan of Ad-Rock,

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.198
and they just -- I was like,
"What is going on

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.133
in the world outside of
suburban Texas?"

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.736
And Spike Jonze is
one of my favorite filmmakers,

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.805
so it was just like
that meme of eating popcorn.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.173
Like, I couldn't get enough.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.707
It could have gone on
for two more hours.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:24.377
-I love those guys so much.
-Me too.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.613
-I read somewhere that
you used to write songs to them

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.680
when you were a little kid.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:33.018
Do you remember doing this?

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.720
-Oh, this is so humbling.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.258
I started writing poetry
when I was 7 or 8.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.625
-Wow.

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:45.064
-And my first poem was called
"Kingdoms in Conflict."

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.665
Started with some
light subject matter there.

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:47.767
Just keeping it light.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.769
-7 years old?
"Kingdoms in Conflict."

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:53.639
-And my older brother
actually found it,

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.441
which, for me,
was like, obviously,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.042
my biggest nightmare
at that time,

00:02:57.042 --> 00:03:01.648
because I was fully expecting
him to just, like, lacerate me.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.648
-Yeah. Read it
in front of everybody.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.718
-As big brothers
are supposed to do.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:09.755
And he read it
and he was just like, "Wow.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.256
Okay, man."
-"This kid's deep.

00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:12.792
Matt's on a different level."
-"This is pretty deep.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.126
Go ahead.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:16.596
You go do -- You go have your
kingdoms in conflict.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.731
I'll be here with my G.I. Joes
when you're ready.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.232
-Oh, that would be a great song.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.602
-I think it should be
the title of our JFK biopic.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.536
It's going to be
"Kingdoms in Conflict."

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:26.672
-Again, someone is watching
this writing

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:27.773
"Kingdoms in Conflict."

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.575
And I can't wait
for you to be in it,

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:32.344
because, honestly,
when you win your Oscar for it,

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.413
you have to just -- You don't
even have to say my name.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:35.581
You don't even
have to say my name.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.550
Just straighten
your bow tie or something.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.718
I'll know it's for me.
I'll know it's for me.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.820
-I'll just --
I'm going to just, like,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.922
bring up a picture of you

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.924
and just put it
in front of your picture

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.359
and walk offstage.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.893
-No. I want you to do that,

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.496
and then I'll know
we have this forever, this bond.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.398
And then we'll come on the show.
We'll talk about it.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.867
We'll show this clip.
That's the way it all works.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.602
Last time, I think we talked --

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.304
You were talking about
"The Boys in the Band"

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.405
on Broadway.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.473
-Yes.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.475
-It was a play
that you guys revived.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:05.511
And you actually won a Tony.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.181
And you're now in this film.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.950
It's a Netflix film
with the exact same cast.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.119
-Yes.
-Can you set up what it's about?

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:16.222
-Yeah. It's about
this group of eight guys

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.324
who all gather together
for a birthday party

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.360
at an apartment
in New York in 1968,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.928
just pre-Stonewall.

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.730
It's a group of
eight gay friends.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:29.501
And the arrival of an
unexpected visitor/interloper

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.637
sort of throws
the whole night into chaos

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:34.373
and calls all the relationships
with themselves and each other

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.709
and society into question.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.712
And, at the same time, it's,
also, I think, really funny.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.947
So it's got a little something
for everybody.

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:44.150
-I loved it.
I thought it was fantastic.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.386
It was well done.
And what a cast, too.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.487
-I love those guys, man.

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:50.823
We had the best time
on Broadway.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:54.327
We were that cast that, like,
came to the stage door early

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.763
to hang out with each other
and hung out afterwards.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.998
We had epic karaoke nights,
where I would get

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.567
different glam-rock wigs
for us to wear.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.737
And I think that sense of
ensemble that you kind of earn,

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.906
as you know from being on
something like "SNL,"

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.174
from doing this show live
eight times a week,

00:05:09.174 --> 00:05:11.110
I think we were able to kind of
bring that to the film.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.879
-Yeah. It's good stuff.
I love it so much.

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.848
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.917
Here are Matt Bomer
and Jim Parsons in

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.385
"The Boys in the Band."

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.053
Take a look at this.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.722
-You in a blue funk
because of the doctor?

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.790
-Christ, no.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.725
I was depressed
long before I got there.

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:28.260
-Well, this should pick you up.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.398
I went shopping today and
I bought all sorts of goodies.

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:35.535
Look. Sandalwood soap.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.504
-I feel better already.
-Mm-hmm. Got in here...

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.773
Oh, your very own toothbrush,

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.108
because I am sick to death
of you using mine.

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.677
-How do you think I feel?

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.445
-You've had worse things
in your mouth.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.347
Oh, also for you.

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.316
Something called Control.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.117
Notice nowhere
is it called hair spray.

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:53.485
Just simply Control

00:05:53.485 --> 00:05:56.722
and the words "for man"
written about 37 times

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:58.524
all over the goddamn can.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.126
-It's called butch assurance.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:03.629
-Well, it's still hair spray,
no matter if they call it Balls.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.131
-Matt Bomer.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:09.168
"The Boys in the Band" is
streaming right now on Netflix.

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.938
I want to hear when
you get this Kennedy script.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.806
I want to hear about
the Tom Brady script.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.508
We have lots of things
to catch up with,

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:16.909
and you're one of our favorites.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.010
Thanks for coming on the show.
I appreciate it, buddy.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.178
-Same, man.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.979
Thank you so much
and thank you for all the laughs

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:22.215
over the past
several months, man.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.782
It's really gotten me
through a lot,

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:24.884
so I really appreciate it.

